IMPORT prelude

-- Row il-63. NOUNS of the one thing this row records (item I1): a citation in one provision of the Banking (Service to Customer) Law, 5741-1981, to a subsection of another, and what that subsection holds.
-- TARGET COMPILER: main. No REFUSE, no section GIVEN, no TYPICALLY, no YMD, no sets: what the sources do not answer is not asked.
--
-- This row is NOT an encoding of the Banking (Service to Customer) Law, 5741-1981. It records one reference, as typed values the tests check, and keeps the defect as an expected-red test.
-- THE KINDS BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's: each is a short plain description I wrote from reading the citing words and the target, so that two descriptions of the same thing are the same kind.
-- The words of the texts are quoted beside each value in the references module: `src:` lines are the Law's consolidation (an excerpt, deposited), `ext:[...]` lines are typed from a page image of the official instrument.
-- A reference whose two descriptions differ is a defect, and is kept in an expected-red file.

§ `Nouns of a cross-reference`

-- Where a reading comes from, from the strongest to the weakest.
DECLARE `Where a reading comes from` IS ONE OF
    `the official page, read from its image, and the cropped image is deposited`
    `the consolidation only`

-- What a provision holds, or what a citation says a provision holds. Three descriptions are enough for this row.
DECLARE `What a reference points at` IS ONE OF
    `the definition of the term financial activity`
    `the definitions of the terms the section uses`
    `a power of the Governor, with the consent of the Minister of Finance, to determine that the section does not apply to a bank, applies to it later, or applies to it only in part`

DECLARE `A subsection of the section on moving financial activity` HAS
    `the label printed` IS A STRING
    `what it holds` IS A `What a reference points at`
    `it contains the definition of the term financial activity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

DECLARE `A cross-reference` HAS
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the citing words name` IS A STRING
    `the label the citing words name` IS A STRING
    `the citing words say it points at` IS A `What a reference points at`
    `the target is` IS A `What a reference points at`
    `the label of the subsection that holds what the citing words say` IS A STRING
    `how many things the citing words name` IS A NUMBER
    `how many of them the target has` IS A NUMBER
    `limb (a) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `limb (b) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

§ `Nouns of a printed citation`

-- The words an instrument inserts, and the words the consolidation prints at the same place, as two values that can be compared.
DECLARE `A printed citation` HAS
    `what the words are` IS A STRING
    `the words` IS A STRING
    `the citation in the words` IS A STRING
    `they were read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
